set('BUY-01','COMPLETE',"Demand now starts with MATERIALS. A requisition was a title, a value and a project — it could not say what was needed, how much, in what unit or by when, and it labelled money `$` while the company record says AED. Two things were built and they do different jobs. IDENTITY: a material master (migration 0333) inside the authority migration 0304 already declared — “the authority for a part is Inventory” — separating WHAT a thing is from WHERE any of it happens to be, because a stock item carried code, name and unit together with warehouse and quantity_on_hand, so a material that had never been stocked had nowhere to exist. `code` and `uom` are immutable: the code is what a person types off a shelf label and the key every existing reference resolved on, and the unit is what a quantity MEANS — change `m` to `roll` and every balance and open demand is reinterpreted with nobody editing a number. Name, specification, make and model stay freely correctable. DESCRIPTION: a requisition line (migration 0335) holds `material_id` forever AND copies the code, name, specification, make, model and unit when it is authored. The reference answers “is the thing installed the thing that was approved and bought”; the copy answers “what did we think we were ordering, when we ordered it” — a reference alone would let a catalogue edit rewrite history, a copy alone is the free text this wave exists to remove. The unit is never typed; it comes from the master, so ten is always ten of something the catalogue counts that way. AN UNPRICED LINE LEAVES THE REQUISITION WITH NO VALUE, not zero and not the partial sum shown as a total, because the value decides WHO MAY APPROVE IT and a missing estimate would buy a weaker approval with absent data — the same defect shape as an absent quantity declaring an order complete. That rule governs rather than merely reports: submission and approval both refuse an incomplete requisition, the approval matrix resolves on the derived value rather than the header a line-based requisition leaves at 0, and the drafted purchase order inherits the same figure. Lines freeze at submission, because approving one thing and buying another is what an editable basis allows.","Auth-ON HTTP and browser proof against PostgreSQL, with JWT on throughout. AUTHORITY: the Storekeeper owns the catalogue and the Buyer is refused creating a material (403) while reading it freely; a duplicate code is refused 409 naming what already holds it; changing a code or a unit is refused 400 rather than silently dropped — they are declared in the DTO precisely so they can be refused, since the global whitelist pipe strips an undeclared field and would have answered 200 with no change. LINEAGE: a line copies the whole description from the master; the unit comes from the material; an unresolvable material leaves the requisition empty; an obsolete material is refused on new demand (409) while the line already citing it stays readable, because retirement speaks about future demand and not about the past; and CORRECTING THE CATALOGUE AFTERWARDS DOES NOT REWRITE WHAT THE REQUISITION MEANT — the line keeps the old name, specification and model while still pointing at the same material. CODING: a cost node from another project is refused, a WBS id offered as a cost code is refused even on the right project, and an ABSENT coding authority refuses rather than passes. VALUE: 6,400 derived from two lines; NO value while one is unpriced, with the priced part reported as progress and the offending line named; submission and approval both refused while incomplete, and the requisition stays a draft so its author can finish it. NEXT-ROLE RECEIPT: the requisition is absent from the approvals inbox before submission and present after it as “Purchase Request / Approve” carrying 6,400 — the figure its lines establish — and approving it drafts the purchase order at that same value rather than at the header’s zero. Two authority corrections were needed to reach that receipt and are recorded rather than buried: the status route derived `procurement.purchase-request.status`, which no shipped role grants, and the service asserted `procurement.pr.approve` for EVERY status change — so a requisition could only be SENT for approval by somebody who could already approve it, making maker/checker unreachable by construction. Submission is now `procurement.pr.update` and the decision stays `procurement.pr.approve`; a holder of update submits and is refused both the approval and the rejection. BROWSER: materials in their own units (12 nr, 250 m), AED on every figure, an unpriced line showing “1 of 2 lines are not priced — this requisition has no value yet”, a zero quantity refused in the domain’s own words, and the row’s own Value column reading AED 6,400 after a reload — one requisition, one total. ACTUAL OUTPUT, per the frozen definition “file, message, calculation or audit event where the capability produces one”: the derived requisition total, a calculation, carried into the approval decision and the drafted order. PERSISTENCE: both tables RLS ENABLED and FORCED with a policy, verified live on a database rebuilt from zero (267 tenant-scoped tables, all enabled, forced and policied). ACCEPTED LIMITS: purchase-order lines do not exist yet, so a requisition line does not yet continue into the order it drafts — that is the next slice; a material bought for direct site delivery is representable but stock positions are not yet keyed on the master (migration 0334 adds the reference, deliberately un-backfilled, because matching legacy positions by code would be a guess written into a reference column); and the error-taxonomy fitness gate reads throw-statement literals, so a refusal composed in a domain function and thrown elsewhere is invisible to it — recorded, not repaired here.");
for (const layer of ['domain','persistence','api','permissions','ui','actualOutput','browser','handoff']) caps.find(c=>c.id==='BUY-01').layers[layer]='COMPLETE';
set('AWD-05','COMPLETE','Fresh Wave 3 proof maps a frozen sold item from Project 360 to a persisted WBS node. Projects derives handover, source, revision and item identity from the immutable snapshot; the outbox reactor posts SOLD quantity once to the quantity ledger. Browser replay with forged source fields resolves to the same canonical mapping.','Regression keeps browser mapping, wrong-project denial, canonical source derivation, idempotent SOLD projection and project/functional authorization green.','handoff');
