 acceptanceProof:'FROZEN MODEL, to be proved rather than assumed: a supplier quotation is an IMMUTABLE FAMILY (supplier + RFQ) containing one or more OFFERS (a base offer and any technical alternatives), each carrying an append-only chain of immutable REVISIONS; a materially different technical or commercial alternative is a separate OFFER and never a revision, so a Bosch equivalent cannot silently replace a Hikvision offer. Once a revision is received its commercial facts are immutable — a change creates the next revision, never an UPDATE of a price. Exactly ONE revision per offer may be commercially effective, enforced by a PARTIAL UNIQUE INDEX over un-superseded rows, with the supersede written BEFORE the insert (SUP-01 proved both halves of that the hard way, in PostgreSQL, after twenty in-memory tests passed). Lifecycle stored as DRAFT, RECEIVED, CONFIRMED, SUPERSEDED, WITHDRAWN, REJECTED — EXPIRED is DERIVED against the comparison date and never stored, because a revision expired today was live on a June comparison and a stored flag cannot say both. SUP-06 compares the commercially effective revision only, never all revisions as competing offers; a family with NO effective revision — withdrawn, or captured and never confirmed — appears in the comparison as UNKNOWN(no_confirmed_revision) and is NEVER silently omitted, because a supplier vanishing from a comparison is the failure nobody notices. A buyer may override which revision is effective only with a recorded reason, actor and timestamp, and the override must be VISIBLE on screen and in the PDF rather than merely stored. Every comparison row carries its revision provenance — quotation reference, offer, revision number and id, received date, validity — so the sheet reads “Supplier A, Q-1001 Rev 2, received 15 Sep 2026” and not merely “Supplier A — AED 95”. Superseded revisions stay readable, with a diff between them, since the move from 92 + freight to 95 + free freight is commercial information a buyer needs. And the two live defects are fixed: the header capture permission is one a Buyer holds, proved Auth-ON, and the refused Lead days input is gone. Proved with a Buyer on screen against PostgreSQL, not through the API.',
