 id:'PO-01',
 title:'A purchase order line cannot record a discount, so a discounted offer cannot be awarded at the price agreed',
 capabilityIds:['SUP-14','BUY-05'],
 classification:'PARTIAL',
 kind:'fresh finding — discovered while building the award (SUP-14)',
 status:'OPEN',
 roles:['Procurement Manager / Buyer','Commercial Manager / QS','Finance'],
 stages:['Procurement'],
 authority:'Procurement purchase-order lines',
 currentBehavior:'A quotation line carries `lineDiscount` and QC-01 captures it; a purchase-order line has quantity and unit price and nothing else, and `orderTotal` — the value that GOVERNS an order with lines — is the sum of quantity x unit price with no discount term. So a supplier who quotes 100 a unit less 5% can be compared correctly and cannot be ordered from correctly. Migration 0354 added a `line_discount` column to `aura_procurement_purchase_order_lines` in anticipation; nothing reads or writes it, and the domain has no field for it. SUP-14 therefore REFUSES to award an offer whose lines carry a discount, naming what is missing, rather than taking either of the two available wrong answers: dropping the discount (ordering at more than was agreed) or folding it into the unit price (restating the per-unit figure the supplier will invoice, which then fails the three-way match against their invoice). The refusal is deliberate and is not the fix.',
 expectedOperationalBehavior:'An order line records the discount the supplier gave, and every figure derived from that line — the order total, the receipt valuation, the invoice match — reads the same discounted value.',
 evidence:'FRESH discovery while building SUP-14: modules/procurement/src/domain/purchase-order-line.ts orderTotal/orderGoverningValue (no discount term); modules/procurement/src/domain/quotation-line.ts lineDiscount; infrastructure/migrations/0354_award_preserves_supplier_terms.sql (column added, unread); modules/procurement/src/sourcing-award.service.ts (the refusal).',
 severity:'MEDIUM',
 remediationDependency:'None upstream. It does NOT block SUP-14: an award of an undiscounted offer is complete and proved. It bounds what SUP-14 can award, and it is why the award refuses instead of guessing.',
