 acceptanceProof:'PASSED. CAPTURE: a Buyer opens a quotation, records currency, tax treatment and rate, freight and terms, payment terms and validity, and prices the requirements — all Auth-ON under r-procurement, refused for a Site Engineer and for an anonymous caller. REFUSED AT CAPTURE, while the supplier’s document is still in front of the person typing: a tax-inclusive price with no rate, a currency AURA cannot govern a rate for, and a lead time on the header naming the line it belongs on. HISTORY: three revisions captured through the UI survive as three, with the diff reading “freight amount: 500 → 0” and “freight terms: EXW → DAP Dubai”, and it survives a reload because it is the server’s. WITHDRAWAL: the current offer withdrawn leaves NO current offer, stated in words, with the earlier revisions still present and still superseded. ALTERNATIVE: added as a separate offer, and the base offer kept its own current revision. AGAINST REAL POSTGRESQL: promoting without demoting is rejected by the partial unique index and the transaction rolls back leaving the earlier revision untouched; five non-confirmed revisions coexist on one offer; a second base offer is refused while alternatives are unbounded; a received revision cannot be rewritten because the SQL predicate itself carries AND status = ‘draft’; and one tenant cannot see another’s quotations. BACKFILL: census first, then counts, VALUES and LINEAGE verified — 12 → 12 across families, base offers, migrated revisions, confirmed and lines bound, with zero commercial-value mismatches and zero orphans — idempotent on a second run, and Rev 0 marked origin = legacy_migration so it cannot read as the supplier’s own. END TO END ON SCREEN: a EUR offer inclusive of 5% tax, 12 units at 126 with a 21-day lead time, made the current offer, reads in the comparison as 480.00 AED per unit and 5,760.00 AED for the line at the governed rate effective 2026-02-01. SUP-01 RE-PROVED on revisions: the verdict, and its outbound handoff to the Buyer with two real actors. Regression 263 procurement, 31 API e2e and 10 browser specs run together at applied: 352. ONE THING WENT WRONG AND IS RECORDED RATHER THAN SMOOTHED: a first draft of 0352 set NOT NULL and dropped the column as separate statements, was HAND-APPLIED through psql outside the runner’s per-file transaction, met two fixture rows the backfill had never seen, failed on the first and dropped the column anyway — destroying the only lineage those rows had. They were deleted, because an unattributable price is not evidence. The migration now opens with a guard that refuses while any line lacks a revision, and the lesson recorded in the file is the hand-application, not the SQL. NOT CLAIMED: Excel/CSV import, PDF extraction and inbound email ingestion, which are stages B, C and D and are not built; and aura_procurement_rfq_quotes is untouched, still carrying the award path and the legacy header scalar lowestQuote compares, which belongs to SUP-13.',
